1
00:00:00,300 --> 00:00:03,800
Space missions are chains of trade-offs.

2
00:00:04,000 --> 00:00:07,200
In a textbook you cannot see the chain.

3
00:00:07,500 --> 00:00:09,800
In Threadline, you can.

4
00:00:10,300 --> 00:00:14,000
You are Mission Director
for a Moon orbiter.

5
00:00:14,300 --> 00:00:19,300
Three instruments, one launcher,
a power system, and a budget.

6
00:00:19,600 --> 00:00:24,500
Variants change one number,
so you can replay.

7
00:00:25,300 --> 00:00:30,500
Every choice draws a thread
to the meters it moves:

8
00:00:30,700 --> 00:00:36,000
weight, power, cost, fuel,
data and science.

9
00:00:36,500 --> 00:00:42,500
Each thread has an icon and a pattern,
not just a colour,

10
00:00:42,800 --> 00:00:49,700
and every change is also
described in words.

11
00:00:50,300 --> 00:00:53,500
Launch.

12
00:00:54,000 --> 00:00:58,500
The mission flies orbit by orbit.

13
00:01:05,300 --> 00:01:08,500
A solar storm arrives.

14
00:01:08,800 --> 00:01:14,300
One decision, three answers,
each with its cost and its risk.

15
00:01:14,600 --> 00:01:18,800
There is no recommended answer.

16
00:01:19,000 --> 00:01:24,800
The best one depends on
the design you built.

17
00:01:25,300 --> 00:01:29,500
The outcome traces back
to your choices.

18
00:01:29,800 --> 00:01:36,000
A Science Card explains the idea
and shows its sources.

19
00:01:36,500 --> 00:01:43,500
What the game simplifies
is said plainly.

20
00:01:45,200 --> 00:01:48,800
Rewind: same seed, same luck,
only my decision changes.

21
00:01:49,000 --> 00:01:51,500
The diff shows what it did.

22
00:01:51,800 --> 00:01:54,800
Then share a link to
challenge a friend.

23
00:01:55,200 --> 00:01:56,500
Try it.

24
00:01:56,800 --> 00:01:59,800
Independent project,
not affiliated with NASA.
